Post-AGI Alpha Hunt =E2=80=94 10 September 2026

Highest-signal new rabbit holes this run

   1. LARGE-FORMAT PHOTOMASK RESET =E2=80=94 a standards transition can str=
and an
   entire equipment ecosystem
   ASML + TSMC formally launched an industry initiative on Sept 8 to move
   High-NA EUV from today=E2=80=99s 6-inch masks toward 12-inch masks, targ=
eting a
   pilot line by 2031 and production readiness by 2033. Intel/ASML separate=
ly
   say the transition requires changes across mask makers, automation
   suppliers, EDA, materials, and fabs. This is not just a demand-growth
   story: it creates a forced replacement/refit cycle and potential
   obsolescence for equipment that cannot scale to the new mask format.

Alpha shape: buy suppliers whose know-how transfers to 12-inch while
shorting/avoiding installed-base economics trapped in 6-inch
infrastructure. Cross-world longs include HOYA/AGC (EUV blanks) and
Lasertec-like mask inspection if their tool roadmaps qualify for the larger
format. HOYA=E2=80=99s 2026 integrated report says it intends to retain
first-supplier position in leading-edge EUV and expand for
High-NA/Hyper-NA, with a new Singapore plant starting FY28 and ~=C2=A542bn
initial investment.

Falsifier: industry decides stitching economics are acceptable and 12-inch
adoption slips materially beyond 2033, or mask/tool suppliers commoditize
the format transition.
Sources:
https://pr.cld.tsmc.com/english/news/3338
https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/newsroom/news/intel-foundry/intel-f=
oundry-asml-accelerate-industry-readiness-for-high-na-euv.html
https://www.hoya.com/ir/2026/en/review/it.html

   1. DNA SYNTHESIS AS THE PHYSICAL COMPILER FOR AI BIOLOGY
   AI can generate sequences essentially for free; useful biology still
   requires those sequences to be physically written, expressed and tested.
   Twist launched Complex Genes in May specifically citing AI-guided protei=
n
   design; it says the service can accept ~99.5% of clonal-gene orders and
   sequences up to 7kb. Its June-quarter filing showed genes shipped up 56%=
 to
   369,000 and revenue +23% y/y, but the company remains loss-making.

The stronger thesis is not =E2=80=98Twist wins AI drug discovery.=E2=80=99 =
It is: as
sequence-generation cost collapses, the scarce layer is translating bits
into reliable DNA at scale. That is a compiler layer shared across many
competing AI-biology models.

Candidate exposure: TWST is the clean public pure-play; Danaher has IDT but
diluted exposure; GenScript offers another route. TWST is financially
risky: Q3 revenue $118.4m, net loss ~$35m. This is a bottleneck candidate,
not a valuation conclusion.

Falsifier: AI-designed sequences remain experimentally low-yield, demand
does not translate into synthesis volume, or in-house/on-benchtop synthesis
destroys centralized provider economics.
Sources:
https://investors.twistbioscience.com/news-releases/news-release-details/tw=
ist-bioscience-expands-clonal-genes-offering-include-long-and
https://www.reuters.com/business/healthcare-pharmaceuticals/amazon-launches=
-ai-research-tool-speed-early-stage-drug-discovery-2026-04-14/

   1. CROs MAY BE A WORLD-STATE CONSISTENCY ARBITRAGE, NOT AN AI SHORT
   Reuters reported in March that IQVIA, Medpace and Charles River sold off
   partly on fears AI agents would let pharma internalize CRO work, while
   experts argued patient recruitment, site operations and regulatory
   execution remain difficult to automate. Since then ICON has partnered wi=
th
   Anthropic and Advarra: the latter connects ICON to technology used by
   >50,000 investigators, including 90% of NCI-designated cancer centers.

The non-obvious world-state contradiction: if AI really generates many more
viable drug candidates faster, physical clinical-development throughput may
become MORE valuable even while administrative CRO labor is automated. The
winning asset may be the site/patient network and proprietary operational
data, not billable human hours.

Candidates: ICLR, IQV, MEDP. Prefer companies where network/data share of
moat is high and human-hour revenue share can shrink without destroying
margins.

Falsifier: pharma internalizes trial operations faster than candidate
volume expands, regulators accept synthetic/in-silico evidence as
substitutes for human trials, or AI creates enough site/recruitment
efficiency that trial-network scarcity disappears.
Sources:
https://www.reuters.com/business/healthcare-pharmaceuticals/ai-led-selloff-=
contract-research-firms-may-be-misjudging-disruption-risk-2026-03-31/
https://www.iconplc.com/news-events/press-releases/icon-and-advarra-introdu=
ce-new-research-ready-connected-site-network
https://www.iconplc.com/news-events/press-releases/icon-announces-multi-yea=
r-collaboration-anthropic-bring-ai-clinical

   1. PROBE CARDS / TEST INTERFACES LOOK LIKE A =E2=80=98HARDWARE SUBSCRIPT=
ION=E2=80=99 ON
   AI COMPLEXITY
   TrendForce=E2=80=99s June probe-card work says AI packaging is reshaping=
 the
   market, order visibility has stretched from ~1 quarter to as much as 2
   years, and consumable probe tips create recurring repair/replacement
   economics. Today, reports say Nvidia is locking high-end test-interface
   capacity while fabs validate second sources. This is exactly the
   experimental-scarcity thesis, but with a better business model than one-=
off
   capital tools.

Candidates: Technoprobe, FormFactor, MPI, MJC; investigate smaller
Taiwanese entrants CHPT/WinWay for convexity. Separate wafer probe,
final-test sockets, HBM and photonics exposure rather than treating them as
one market.

Falsifier: advanced packaging test becomes substantially
parallelized/standardized, probe-card ASPs fall despite AI complexity, or
second-source qualification removes scarcity faster than end demand grows.
Sources:
https://www.trendforce.com/research/download/RP260626XO3
https://www.formfactor.com/ (company materials should be used for follow-up=
)

   1. QUALIFICATION LATENCY IS A MOAT =E2=80=94 THE MATERIAL MAY BE COMMODI=
TY, THE
   QUALIFIED MATERIAL IS NOT
   China began collecting provisional deposits of 80.8%-99.2% on Japanese
   dichlorosilane from Sept 8. DCS is a thin-film deposition precursor. The
   interesting signal is not the tariff itself: semiconductor-grade materia=
ls
   require extreme purity, container control, analytical capability and
   fab-specific qualification. A political shock can reprice supply
   immediately; customer qualification cannot move at political speed.

This suggests a new kernel variable:
QualifiedCapacity =3D physical capacity =C3=97 purity capability =C3=97 cus=
tomer
qualification =C3=97 geographic accessibility.

Raw tonnes are misleading. The alpha is in suppliers with already-qualified
capacity in the right geography.

Candidates: Shin-Etsu, Nippon Sanso, Air Liquide/Denal, Korean
specialty-gas suppliers such as TEMC; Solvay is separately doubling
ultra-pure H2O2 capacity in Taiwan by end-2026 to >70kt/yr because
wafer-cleaning purity demand is rising.

Falsifier: Chinese fabs qualify domestic DCS rapidly with no yield penalty,
or end-user inventory makes the trade action economically irrelevant.
Sources:
https://apnews.com/article/ea58c95c47481c5c822a3a544e6b68cc
https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/solvay-more-than-double-taiwan-c=
hip-peroxide-capacity-targets-tripling-2026-09-03/

   1. PROCUREMENT RIGHTS ARE BECOMING REAL OPTIONS
   JLL=E2=80=99s 2026 data-center outlook says 57% of projects experienced =
delays
   of 3+ months in 2025; US equipment lead times average ~42 weeks, 83% abo=
ve
   2019, and developers are pre-ordering some materials 24 months ahead and
   holding 6-12 months of strategic inventory. Once delivery slots are scar=
ce,
   a manufacturer=E2=80=99s booked slot or a developer=E2=80=99s reserved a=
llocation becomes
   an economically valuable option even before the underlying equipment exi=
sts.

Kernel implication: add capacity_reservation_value and
cancellation/transferability to bottleneck scoring. Backlog quality should
distinguish firm orders, reservation deposits, cancellable slots and
speculative queue positions.

Falsifier: equipment capacity additions collapse lead times rapidly or
reservations prove non-transferable/cancellable with little economic value.
Source:
https://www.jll.com/content/dam/jllcom/en/global/documents/reports/research=
-reports/26-research-global-data-center-outlook-new.pdf

Research priority for next pass
The most interesting of these is the 12-inch mask reset because it
combines: forced standards migration + huge installed-base implications +
small upstream suppliers + a multi-year timetable that public markets may
not model explicitly. I would next map every 6x12-mask dependency: blank
substrate, multilayer coating, resist, writer, inspection, cleaning,
pellicle, mask handling, stockers, transport pods, EDA field assumptions
and scanner interfaces, then score each supplier for transferability vs
stranded-capital risk.

Second priority: DNA synthesis + CRO/site networks as a single AI-biology
scarcity chain: model-generated sequence =E2=86=92 synthesis =E2=86=92 assa=
y =E2=86=92
animal/preclinical =E2=86=92 patient/site =E2=86=92 regulatory evidence. Th=
e value should
migrate down that chain as each preceding stage gets automated.

